         "displayName" : "Lewis Pringle",
         "self" : "https://stroika.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/user?accountId=557058%3A4fe560ca-b4e1-41d1-9bdf-97b1684eda32",
         "timeZone" : "America/New_York"
      },
      "customfield_10001" : "1_*:*_1_*:*_13847385_*|*_3_*:*_1_*:*_161640302757_*|*_5_*:*_1_*:*_0",
      "customfield_10012" : "0|i003an:",
      "customfield_10300" : "{}",
      "description" : {
         "content" : [
            {
               "content" : [
                  {
                     "text" : "We CURRENTLY have a new bug (not a regression but a new regression test) - where we get helgrind failures.",
                     "type" : "text"
                  }
               ],
               "type" : "paragraph"
            },
            {
               "content" : [
                  {
                     "text" : "regtest 37",
                     "type" : "text"
                  }
               ],
               "type" : "paragraph"
            },
            {
               "content" : [
                  {
                     "text" : "Test9_MutlipleThreadsReadingUnsynchonizedContainer_",
                     "type" : "text"
                  },
                  {
                     "type" : "hardBreak"
                  },
                  {
                     "text" : "Test10_MutlipleThreadsReadingOneUpdateUsingSynchonizedContainer_",
                     "type" : "text"
                  }
               ],
               "type" : "paragraph"
            },
            {
               "content" : [
                  {
                     "text" : "Discussed with KDJ/Sterling",
                     "type" : "text"
                  }
               ],
               "type" : "paragraph"
            },
            {
               "content" : [
                  {
                     "text" : "I think the plan is to make an OPTIONAL param to containers like Sequnece_Array - if iterators are autosafe-patching.",
                     "type" : "text"
                  }
               ],
               "type" : "paragraph"
            },
            {
               "content" : [
                  {
                     "text" : "THEN - its the responsabity of the callers to assure iterator acessed syncrhonzed with the owning container (patch but not lcoking other than debug::assertexternalylsynconized)",
                     "type" : "text"
                  }
               ],
               "type" : "paragraph"
            },
            {
               "content" : [
                  {
                     "text" : "But most of the stroika code - loses the patching logic. So runs FASTER (and more bug free)",
                     "type" : "text"
                  }
               ],
               "type" : "paragraph"
            },
            {
               "content" : [
                  {
                     "text" : "Maybe include in DEBUG mode maintaining the linked list (or something similar) to DETECT bugs and assert out. Maybe on iteartor have a CHANGE COUNT. And then to assert in iterator that they cannot be used after a change to the owning container!",
                     "type" : "text"
                  }
               ],
               "type" : "paragraph"
            },
            {
               "content" : [
                  {
                     "text" : "Conssider i = s.begin();",
                     "type" : "text"
                  },
                  {
                     "type" : "hardBreak"
                  },
                  {
                     "text" : "s.append([x]);",
                     "type" : "text"
                  },
                  {
                     "type" : "hardBreak"
                  },
                  {
                     "text" : "i++; // assert ciz s 'changed'.",
                     "type" : "text"
                  }
               ],
               "type" : "paragraph"
            },
            {
               "content" : [
                  {
                     "text" : "ALSO - make Remove() method on Sequnce (and maybe others) return an Iterator to next item.",
                     "type" : "text"
                  }
               ],
               "type" : "paragraph"
            }
         ],
         "type" : "doc",
         "version" : 1
      },
